# Raw photo directories only (BUILD-ORDER 0.0). Never ignore markdown, scripts, or docx.
# These are camera/site photo dumps under directories literally named "Photos" (and
# variants like "Photos 2"). Repo was 13G with these included; ~7.4G of that is here.
#
# Written as "contents of Photos folders" rather than "Photos folders", because git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded. The old `**/Photos*/`
# form silently swallowed 21 GUIDE.md files living inside Photos folders, including
# the one that ships in the job template, against this file's own "never ignore
# markdown" rule (found and fixed 2026-08-09).
**/Photos*/**
!**/Photos*/GUIDE.md

# macOS Finder noise (untracked 2026-07-07). Never contains project content.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Python bytecode (Phase 2f, 2026-07-19). Regenerated on every script run; never project content.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/

# Web app build artifacts (Task 8, 2026-08-09). Installed/built, never project content.
app/web/node_modules/
app/web/dist/

# Test-runner cache (2026-08-09). Regenerated on every pytest run; never project content.
.pytest_cache/

# Mark's demo job folders (copied in 2026-08-12), so development and testing run
# against real job folders instead of invented ones. They are his working files,
# never project content, and the app treats them as read-only inputs.
RRF Demo Jobs/

# The demo testing tool, for this machine only. Never shipped to Mark.
# .rrf-demo.json turns it on and names the approved paths; without it the reset
# button does not render and the endpoint answers 404.
# The baseline is frozen evidence. Staging and rollback are working space and
# hold nothing after a successful reset.
.rrf-demo.json
.rrf-demo-baseline/
.rrf-demo-staging/
.rrf-demo-rollback/

# Mark's delivered appraisals and his folder template are his clients' work.
# They stay on the development machine and are never committed here.
Report Examples/
locker/
archive/
training/
testing/
sandbox/

# Local settings and keys, which live in the home folder, never in a project.
.rrf-app.env
.rrf-app.json
*.env
!app/web/.env.example

# The Windows package and its download cache (Task 3, 2026-08-19). Built by
# tools/package_windows.py, carries an embedded interpreter and wheels, and is
# never project content.
build/
runtime.json
